<title>SOUTH AFRICA: VAAL REEFS WARNS OF MAJOR JOB CUTS.</title>
<headline>VAAL REEFS WARNS OF MAJOR JOB CUTS.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Vaal Reefs Exploration and Mining Co warned of major job cuts at the mine's No 3 shaft which continued to incur losses.</p>
<p>&quot;We will have to investigate compulsory retrenchments...we will have to make fairly significant reductions,&quot; mine manager Dick Fisher said at a March quarter results presentation.</p>
<p>The company said the future of the shaft remained in balance and decisive steps would have to be taken soon.</p>
<p>&quot;We anticipate having to withdraw our labour from the No 3 shaft,&quot; Fisher added.</p>
<p>Vaal Reefs produced 16,022 kg of gold in the three months to end-March.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27-11 482 1003</p>
